# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SEO: one URL per page.
#
# The public site is a single page — all in-page navigation uses #hash anchors
# — plus /privacy and the staff /admin app. The old catch-all
# (`/*  /index.html  200`) answered EVERY other path with HTTP 200 and a clone
# of the homepage, which is what fed Search Console the endless stream of
# "Alternate page with proper canonical tag" duplicates of https://hotelitoya.co.ke/
#
# Rules are evaluated top to bottom; the first one that matches wins.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# `/index.html` is a real file in the publish directory, so these need the `!`
# (force) flag. The homepage is only ever reachable as `/`.
/index.html          /           301!
/index.htm           /           301!
/index.php           /           301!

# Alternate / legacy privacy URLs (the footer used to link /privacy-policy)
/privacy/index.html  /privacy    301!
/privacy/            /privacy    301!
/privacy-policy      /privacy    301!

# Staff app — canonical trailing-slash form
/admin/              /admin      301!

# App routes that need a real HTML document on a direct hit.
# /privacy is a built file (privacy/index.html) carrying its own canonical tag.
/privacy             /privacy/index.html   200!
/admin               /index.html           200
/admin/*             /index.html           200

# Everything else falls through to dist/404.html with a genuine HTTP 404
# status, so Google drops unknown URLs instead of filing them as duplicates.

